(T3-deep) OCF = literal path SUM (indep set, sign vector)?
========================================================================
  n=5 tournaments=1024  H==OCF(sum 2^#cycles over indep sets) mismatches=0
  sample (H, OCF): [(1, 1), (1, 1), (3, 3), (1, 1), (1, 1)]
  => If 0 mismatches: H IS a path-integral SUM over (indep cycle set, sign)
     pairs with all amplitudes = +1 (INCOHERENT sum, |1|^2 each). The
     'amplitude' is real & positive -> NO interference in H itself.
  CONTRAST: the WALSH coeffs (-1)^desc DO carry signs, but they live at
  the FOURIER (dual) level, not in the path count. So OCF=incoherent sum;
  the interference is in the Walsh/Fourier dual (THM-071), not in H.

